    "content": "## QA Testing Complete\n\nAll 22 checklist items were tested and recorded. **Summary: 17 PASS / 5 FAIL**\n\n**Failures found:**\n1. **FT-2** – The homepage \"Featured\" section's \"View all\" link routes to `/products?featured=true`, but this query parameter has no effect — it shows all products instead of just featured ones. There's no other way to browse the complete featured set.\n2. **FT-4** – The Tags filter chip list on `/products` is static/hardcoded to the original 35 seed tags. Newly added, renamed, or removed tags on products never update this filter list, even though they correctly appear on the product's detail page and in keyword search.\n3. **FT-19** – No persistence layer exists. Products created/edited via the admin panel are held only in in-memory client state and are lost after a page reload/hard navigation.\n4. **CS-20** – The admin form allows publishing a product with only a name and short description; missing image, retailer link, price, and specifications do not block submission, and the incomplete product becomes immediately visible to visitors.\n5. **IX-21** – On dedicated category pages (e.g. `/category/home`), the category filter dropdown is non-functional — selecting a different category snaps back to the current one instead of navigating/filtering (the same control works fine on `/products`).\n\nAll other functional, constraint, interaction, and content items (browsing, search, sorting/filtering, category assignment, tag CRUD content, product creation/editing content accuracy, detail-page consistency, not-found handling, external retailer links, etc.) passed verification."
  }
